-932f-08763c5ce37a" "question-73f7b139-c8da-5c53-9a35-10e77ca9a819" "question-f0d9aadf-c429-54b7-bed3-89ab52703eb2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-44c1c5d8-2db1-5cbc-a653-89f6c7b7e591" :question/id #uuid "44c1c5d8-2db1-5cbc-a653-89f6c7b7e591" :question/math-academy-id "q-133920" :question/problem "![](images/b5/b5d153746d837a857918028aceb623a5c2b9267f00b6baaceb2f24a8172587ee.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above gives the correspondence between the variables $x$ and $y$ for some data points.\nUse the trend line to predict the value of $y$ when $x=70.$" :question/worked-solution "To make our prediction, we proceed as follows:\n\n- First, we start at $x=70$ on the $x$-axis.\n\n![](images/ee/ee670899ebf962939a77959c58219502907681d8cf84329f402b67f6f09a24ba.png)\n\n* Then, we move up until we intersect the trend line.\n\n![](images/f6/f6d34d0c6b95b4b3d5ecf720346ca1e0008ac86c42e8024a2435e2bf792e5031.png)\n\n- Finally, we move left until we intersect the $y$-axis.\n\n![](images/02/0217edcb171859f1aec207d5c248c483a3147dbe74aed277f1313009dbc317c9.png)\n\nTherefore, when $x=70,$ we obtain $y≈5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-13689481-942b-557a-8a56-b6a42e7e64e0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-13689481-942b-557a-8a56-b6a42e7e64e0" :answer-field/id #uuid "13689481-942b-557a-8a56-b6a42e7e64e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-859eb061-c189-52a9-8d20-8abc934723c6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2ee1dd56-d310-5198-9ca6-fff22149c547" "answer-859eb061-c189-52a9-8d20-8abc934723c6" "answer-f300a523-7514-5583-b6cf-ac152d439a0e" "answer-121e378e-227c-58b4-9178-bd289e4d1481" "answer-2e65ceff-fed4-5dfb-bf7c-85e0da5bc187"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ee1dd56-d310-5198-9ca6-fff22149c547" :answer/id #uuid "2ee1dd56-d310-5198-9ca6-fff22149c547" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-859eb061-c189-52a9-8d20-8abc934723c6" :answer/id #uuid "859eb061-c189-52a9-8d20-8abc934723c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f300a523-7514-5583-b6cf-ac152d439a0e" :answer/id #uuid "f300a523-7514-5583-b6cf-ac152d439a0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-121e378e-227c-58b4-9178-bd289e4d1481" :answer/id #uuid "121e378e-227c-58b4-9178-bd289e4d1481" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e65ceff-fed4-5dfb-bf7c-85e0da5bc187" :answer/id #uuid "2e65ceff-fed4-5dfb-bf7c-85e0da5bc187" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186268933 :question/worked-solution "To make our prediction, we proceed as follows:\n\n- First, we start at $y=20$ on the $y$-axis.\n\n![](images/b6/b614a0ed708e9b0e333c05daf6adde3f4636daebf00f622fc570ade99d8237d8.png)\n\n- Then, we move right until we intersect the trend line.\n\n![](images/d6/d6772acc92fc6b1ed7c9efbeb4a292ec21f5d2b8069bd0fa4ad7a8d5f7d79470.png)\n\n- Finally, we move down until we intersect the $x$-axis.\n\n![](images/39/3916c8c4a6bfa6cb558cfa91e268e66d011659753ca23da0396cf2ed9f8d1a8f.png)\n\nTherefore, when $y=20,$ we obtain $x≈7.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-1b530d38-bb33-510e-b9cb-65e2c39387f5" :question/id #uuid "1b530d38-bb33-510e-b9cb-65e2c39387f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-133883" :question/problem "![](images/df/dff61f08e09f21935f616788e54dfb56e0d0a89f38cce9fbc6dc7333d21ba5f1.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above gives the correspondence between the variables $x$ and $y$ for some data points.\nUse the trend line to predict the value of $x$ when $y=80.$" :question/worked-solution "To make our prediction, we proceed as follows:\n\n- First, we start at $y=80$ on the $y$-axis.\n\n![](images/e5/e5923b6c9f0ac4dcf2aee35e67877c425b44f81830bb9f0865c5e21acf81e3f4.png)\n\n- Then, we move right until we intersect the trend line.\n\n![](images/61/613849314df8014335f7493f9b6b64cb4f2ecd1e585593416f416f1854e12ffa.png)\n\n- Finally, we move down until we intersect the $x$-axis.\n\n![](images/45/4523e742266e3f2d2e759c6e65eb2a7f2bd31e8f4b8473b8e6bfbabec067c9d9.png)\n\nTherefore, when $y=80,$ we obtain $x≈15.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2afd5bb4-fefc-5765-8bdb-316b07bd305a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2afd5bb4-fefc-5765-8bdb-316b07bd305a" :answer-field/id #uuid "2afd5bb4-fefc-5765-8bdb-316b07bd305a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4f5b549b-f313-5f3a-8a10-a2f5214f2bcb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d8b8e27d-8509-52d0-9487-b3bb9fd51889" "answer-4f5b549b-f313-5f3a-8a10-a2f5214f2bcb" "answer-82709572-bf25-533e-94a9-6be94d2c36f4" "answer-623e74da-8a64-5b5e-97fd-8808df31847a" "answer-3ea3c33a-403d-567e-a88d-49804b37e946"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d8b8e27d-8509-52d0-9487-b3bb9fd51889" :answer/id #uuid "d8b8e27d-8509-52d0-9487-b3bb9fd51889" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f5b549b-f313-5f3a-8a10-a2f5214f2bcb" :answer/id #uuid "4f5b549b-f313-5f3a-8a10-a2f5214f2bcb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82709572-bf25-533e-94a9-6be94d2c36f4" :answer/id #uuid "82709572-bf25-533e-94a9-6be94d2c36f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-623e74da-8a64-5b5e-97fd-8808df31847a" :answer/id #uuid "623e74da-8a64-5b5e-97fd-8808df31847a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ea3c33a-403d-567e-a88d-49804b37e946" :answer/id #uuid "3ea3c33a-403d-567e-a88d-49804b37e946" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8bba2235-837e-5ee6-9f31-af7dd59da4b8" :question/id #uuid "8bba2235-837e-5ee6-9f31-af7dd59da4b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-133932" :question/problem "![](images/31/31932ff71e679d32ba3abee0276f7a039e5f204649e63feffeb13029eabc5b88.png)\n\nAn ice cream shop wants to determine the relationship between the outside temperature $x$ (in degrees Celsius) and the number of customers $y$ they serve. The scatter plot above shows the information they collected over several days. The equation of the trend line is $y=2.25x-19.$\n\nEstimate the outside temperature if they served $53$ customers." :question/worked-solution "To predict the outside temperature knowing that they served $53$ customers, we need to substitute $y=53$ into the equation of the trend line and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2.25x-19 \\\\ 53 & =2.25x-19 \\\\ 2.25x & =72 \\\\ x & =32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, according to this model, the outside temperature is approximately ${32}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$\n\nNote: The point where $y=53$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fbc8d1ae-cf76-5d8c-94ef-a0c5ef612072"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fbc8d1ae-cf76-5d8c-94ef-a0c5ef612072" :answer-field/id #uuid "fbc8d1ae-cf76-5d8c-94ef-a0c5ef612072" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bd19dc87-8558-5ba0-9185-3db58ee92bcf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-25c938d8-1dfb-5d3f-8853-61890c9bf0cd" "answer-a2006beb-9a32-58ef-bcfb-45b833c60509" "answer-54bf6e94-edcd-5556-960e-3ae854a3d5a8" "answer-bd19dc87-8558-5ba0-9185-3db58ee92bcf" "answer-2f5d5d01-3161-5cd8-9b54-4a4076db201c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25c938d8-1dfb-5d3f-8853-61890c9bf0cd" :answer/id #uuid "25c938d8-1dfb-5d3f-8853-61890c9bf0cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{31.5}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2006beb-9a32-58ef-bcfb-45b833c60509" :answer/id #uuid "a2006beb-9a32-58ef-bcfb-45b833c60509" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{31}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-54bf6e94-edcd-5556-960e-3ae854a3d5a8" :answer/id #uuid "54bf6e94-edcd-5556-960e-3ae854a3d5a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{32.5}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd19dc87-8558-5ba0-9185-3db58ee92bcf" :answer/id #uuid "bd19dc87-8558-5ba0-9185-3db58ee92bcf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{32}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f5d5d01-3161-5cd8-9b54-4a4076db201c" :answer/id #uuid "2f5d5d01-3161-5cd8-9b54-4a4076db201c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{33}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f611e328-34e9-5ebd-abcf-dae6da9bf9cb" :question/id #uuid "f611e328-34e9-5ebd-abcf-dae6da9bf9cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-133882" :question/problem "![](images/6e/6eb063fffcfd0464cbd8cf79811d9ed2ae1e820a30ec621f50e0cc3b9e150e35.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above gives the correspondence between the variables $x$ and $y$ for some data points.\nThe equation of the trend line is $y=5-0.25x.$ Assuming this trend continues, estimate the value of $y$ when $x=10.$" :question/worked-solution "We can estimate the required value by substituting $x=10$ into the equation of the trend line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =5-0.25x \\\\  & =5-0.25(10) \\\\  & =5-2.5 \\\\  & =2.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, according to this model, when $x=10,$ we have $y≈2.5.$\n\nNote: The point where $x=10$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-75ef87bd-bbc6-5f5c-a6b4-1dd96adfb505"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-75ef87bd-bbc6-5f5c-a6b4-1dd96adfb505" :answer-field/id #uuid "75ef87bd-bbc6-5f5c-a6b4-1dd96adfb505" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b6e1124f-fabb-5356-8775-645e555a22b8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1c1a6631-58bb-5134-9a94-217bbe53ee56" "answer-13f4c61a-c56d-54cd-9ef2-fd5516f7e35b" "answer-43b4d286-1020-595c-82a9-fd0db5f180b8" "answer-b6e1124f-fabb-5356-8775-645e555a22b8" "answer-3da7d80f-588f-5952-bfcd-0334bb39a7f1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c1a6631-58bb-5134-9a94-217bbe53ee56" :answer/id #uuid "1c1a6631-58bb-5134-9a94-217bbe53ee56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13f4c61a-c56d-54cd-9ef2-fd5516f7e35b" :answer/id #uuid "13f4c61a-c56d-54cd-9ef2-fd5516f7e35b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-43b4d286-1020-595c-82a9-fd0db5f180b8" :answer/id #uuid "43b4d286-1020-595c-82a9-fd0db5f180b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b6e1124f-fabb-5356-8775-645e555a22b8" :answer/id #uuid "b6e1124f-fabb-5356-8775-645e555a22b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3da7d80f-588f-5952-bfcd-0334bb39a7f1" :answer/id #uuid "3da7d80f-588f-5952-bfcd-0334bb39a7f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1131d502-6491-586e-9e5c-4aa6c2f2c8de" :question/id #uuid "1131d502-6491-586e-9e5c-4aa6c2f2c8de" :question/math-academy-id "q-133851" :question/problem "![](images/8f/8fb46d101101d3d2bdb4afcfcc1436f1a62137389db2ffc3fde0cff71054e7f1.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above gives the correspondence between the variables $x$ and $y$ for some data points.\nThe equation of the trend line is $y=27-0.5x.$ Assuming this trend continues, estimate the value of $y$ when $x=16.$" :question/worked-solution "We can estimate the required value by substituting $x=16$ into the equation of the trend line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =27-0.5x \\\\  & =27-0.5(16) \\\\  & =27-8 \\\\  & =19\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, according to this model, when $x=16,$ we have $y≈19.$\n\nNote: The point where $x=16$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-657377ca-bf35-54d0-beff-26dc9f7a2c08"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-657377ca-bf35-54d0-beff-26dc9f7a2c08" :answer-field/id #uuid "657377ca-bf35-54d0-beff-26dc9f7a2c08" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4837a9be-da87-5c2a-937a-176ee878175a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b8e7ccce-2e82-5e1e-8aec-fe59da6cffeb" "answer-41b26ab6-dcc5-53e7-b4be-5368fc7fcf38" "answer-4837a9be-da87-5c2a-937a-176ee878175a" "answer-32f64d86-98ef-5369-b4fb-15c220217b15" "answer-558b121a-2eef-5148-999a-63dbe7a14557"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8e7ccce-2e82-5e1e-8aec-fe59da6cffeb" :answer/id #uuid "b8e7ccce-2e82-5e1e-8aec-fe59da6cffeb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "17" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41b26ab6-dcc5-53e7-b4be-5368fc7fcf38" :answer/id #uuid "41b26ab6-dcc5-53e7-b4be-5368fc7fcf38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4837a9be-da87-5c2a-937a-176ee878175a" :answer/id #uuid "4837a9be-da87-5c2a-937a-176ee878175a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "19" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-32f64d86-98ef-5369-b4fb-15c220217b15" :answer/id #uuid "32f64d86-98ef-5369-b4fb-15c220217b15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-558b121a-2eef-5148-999a-63dbe7a14557" :answer/id #uuid "558b121a-2eef-5148-999a-63dbe7a14557" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bf3f9846-0d01-5263-932f-08763c5ce37a" :question/id #uuid "bf3f9846-0d01-5263-932f-08763c5ce37a" :question/math-academy-id "q-133941" :question/problem "![](images/21/2130538a141293fda6b1bf07c1f0e8e5f7c347a2c688074689b1c13583a11bd2.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above gives the correspondence between the variables $x$ and $y$ for some data points. Estimate the value of $y$ when $x=20.$ \n\n*Hint: Assume the trend is linear, and that the trend line passes through the points $(1,23)$ and $(9,27).$*" :question/worked-solution "First, using the hint, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot.\n\n![](images/a0/a00942c18663c8e9ea2dd2c5354bbe177f7f8b35a4568c5234b9c92b844f196a.png)\n\nOur trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(1,23)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(9,27).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{27-23}{9-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{8} \\\\  & =0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=0.5$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=0.5x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to calculate the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can do this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(1,23):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =0.5x+b \\\\ 23 & =0.5(1)+b \\\\ 23 & =0.5+b \\\\ b & =22.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=0.5x+22.5.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $x=20$ into the equation above, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =0.5x+22.5 \\\\  & =0.5(20)+22.5 \\\\  & =10+22.5 \\\\  & =32.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, according to this model, when $x=20$ we have $y≈32.5.$\n\nNote: The point where $x=20$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1a665d06-44a7-566e-9ba1-44800e618b3b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1a665d06-44a7-566e-9ba1-44800e618b3b" :answer-field/id #uuid "1a665d06-44a7-566e-9ba1-44800e618b3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5f18bd76-f921-5ef0-ab74-e55531698dd4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-528ae067-ae5a-58ad-a807-4a32664e9dd8" "answer-5a121c0e-eee5-5094-93d2-ed8591f7049e" "answer-5f18bd76-f921-5ef0-ab74-e55531698dd4" "answer-f96d4a56-8233-583c-bdd1-d33a53b4fcd4" "answer-3177c2c7-aa42-566a-8362-fecceb1e8163"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-528ae067-ae5a-58ad-a807-4a32664e9dd8" :answer/id #uuid "528ae067-ae5a-58ad-a807-4a32664e9dd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a121c0e-eee5-5094-93d2-ed8591f7049e" :answer/id #uuid "5a121c0e-eee5-5094-93d2-ed8591f7049e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "31" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f18bd76-f921-5ef0-ab74-e55531698dd4" :answer/id #uuid "5f18bd76-f921-5ef0-ab74-e55531698dd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f96d4a56-8233-583c-bdd1-d33a53b4fcd4" :answer/id #uuid "f96d4a56-8233-583c-bdd1-d33a53b4fcd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "33" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3177c2c7-aa42-566a-8362-fecceb1e8163" :answer/id #uuid "3177c2c7-aa42-566a-8362-fecceb1e8163" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "34.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-73f7b139-c8da-5c53-9a35-10e77ca9a819" :question/id #uuid "73f7b139-c8da-5c53-9a35-10e77ca9a819" :question/math-academy-id "q-133962" :question/problem "![](images/6f/6f38e64442bb383f218dede5a88740653f958864d3284ce09c3e1bb99ed7e421.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above shows the relationship between the time (in hours) some college students spend studying the night before an exam and the time they spend sleeping that night. Assuming this trend continues, estimate the time a student spends studying if that student gets only $3.75$ hours of sleep.\n\n*Hint: Assume the trend is linear and that the trend line passes through the points $(2,7.5)$ and $(4,5).$*" :question/worked-solution "First, using the hint, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot.\n\n![](images/9e/9e1653b2acbe5c5924e2d562308b2640c64f317ed7500fba4e149c926c9205ab.png)\n\nThe trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(2,7.5)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(4,5).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-7.5}{4-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2.5)}{2} \\\\  & =-1.25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=-1.25$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=-1.25x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to calculate the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can do this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(4,5):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-1.25x+b \\\\ 5 & =-1.25(4)+b \\\\ 5 & =-5+b \\\\ b & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=-1.25x+10.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y=3.75$ into the equation above and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-1.25x+10 \\\\ 3.75 & =-1.25x+10 \\\\ 1.25x & =6.25 \\\\ x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, according to this model, the student spends approximately $5$ hours studying.\n\nNote: The point where $y=3.75$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b6a3ec9d-c696-5081-a8d8-ff61a574a27d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b6a3ec9d-c696-5081-a8d8-ff61a574a27d" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6a3ec9d-c696-5081-a8d8-ff61a574a27d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f8e37f8a-7f29-5bb4-a7b5-9b3b74038eee" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f8e37f8a-7f29-5bb4-a7b5-9b3b74038eee" "answer-41db18df-a534-5726-b39d-8b9562beddc7" "answer-fa18fd73-7cda-5618-806a-041e5424f8a6" "answer-ac1ecf06-594b-58b4-b365-6708b2e5e0ef" "answer-7378e9b9-c866-5489-8c98-278113aa0897"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f8e37f8a-7f29-5bb4-a7b5-9b3b74038eee" :answer/id #uuid "f8e37f8a-7f29-5bb4-a7b5-9b3b74038eee" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$5$ hours" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41db18df-a534-5726-b39d-8b9562beddc7" :answer/id #uuid "41db18df-a534-5726-b39d-8b9562beddc7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$5.25$ hours" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa18fd73-7cda-5618-806a-041e5424f8a6" :answer/id #uuid "fa18fd73-7cda-5618-806a-041e5424f8a6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$5.5$ hours" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac1ecf06-594b-58b4-b365-6708b2e5e0ef" :answer/id #uuid "ac1ecf06-594b-58b4-b365-6708b2e5e0ef" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$5.75$ hours" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7378e9b9-c866-5489-8c98-278113aa0897" :answer/id #uuid "7378e9b9-c866-5489-8c98-278113aa0897" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6$ hours" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f0d9aadf-c429-54b7-bed3-89ab52703eb2" :question/id #uuid "f0d9aadf-c429-54b7-bed3-89ab52703eb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-133942" :question/problem "![](images/9a/9aa9f94a8de990bdb8332f2efd5c8e945c9bec4847855eebc3fe7f6a3a02a175.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above gives the correspondence between the variables $x$ and $y$ for some data points. Estimate the value of $y$ when $x=23.$ \n\n*Hint: Assume the trend is linear, and that the trend line passes through the points $(11,8)$ and $(15,7).$*" :question/worked-solution "First, using the hint, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot.\n\n![](images/b9/b9dbed9bab9d769f7408006854bd0c159cb980bfa5f4441fe1b4e5753dfbc078.png)\n\nOur trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(11,8)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(15,7).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7-8}{15-11} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)}{4} \\\\  & =-0.25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=-0.25$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=-0.25x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to calculate the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can do this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(11,8):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-0.25x+b \\\\ 8 & =-0.25(11)+b \\\\ 8 & =-2.75+b \\\\ b & =10.75\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=-0.25x+10.75.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $x=23$ into the equation above, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-0.25x+10.75 \\\\  & =-0.25(23)+10.75 \\\\  & =-5.75+10.75 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, according to this model, when $x=23$ we have $y≈5.$\n\nNote: The point where $x=23$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-588b06de-dfd6-5c5b-94a0-cddc954cebc9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-588b06de-dfd6-5c5b-94a0-cddc954cebc9" :answer-field/id #uuid "588b06de-dfd6-5c5b-94a0-cddc954cebc9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d3eb3f93-e0e4-5ab6-ab1b-9485d4573bd5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ec03f0fb-5fe8-5b76-ae17-c5f458c1c65c" "answer-0c57330b-8507-5a3c-9806-0e8c205fd13d" "answer-1803bbd6-5355-5d9a-9fb7-f4cf0aaa465d" "answer-d3eb3f93-e0e4-5ab6-ab1b-9485d4573bd5" "answer-a236d02f-5776-5a91-b192-27c106d17a85"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec03f0fb-5fe8-5b76-ae17-c5f458c1c65c" :answer/id #uuid "ec03f0fb-5fe8-5b76-ae17-c5f458c1c65c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c57330b-8507-5a3c-9806-0e8c205fd13d" :answer/id #uuid "0c57330b-8507-5a3c-9806-0e8c205fd13d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1803bbd6-5355-5d9a-9fb7-f4cf0aaa465d" :answer/id #uuid "1803bbd6-5355-5d9a-9fb7-f4cf0aaa465d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3eb3f93-e0e4-5ab6-ab1b-9485d4573bd5" :answer/id #uuid "d3eb3f93-e0e4-5ab6-ab1b-9485d4573bd5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a236d02f-5776-5a91-b192-27c106d17a85" :answer/id #uuid "a236d02f-5776-5a91-b192-27c106d17a85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179896 :activity/expected-seconds 480.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186067318 :answer-field/choices 17592186067319] [:db/retract 17592186067318 :answer-field/choices 17592186067320] [:db/retract 17592186067318 :answer-field/choices 17592186067321] [:db/retract 17592186067318 :answer-field/choices 17592186067322] [:db/retract 17592186067318 :answer-field/choices 17592186067323] [:db/retract 17592186067714 :answer-field/choices 17592186067717] {:db/id 17592186069358 :question/problem "Solve the equation ${3}^{x}=\\frac{1}{27}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite $27$ as ${3}^{3}$ to get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{x} & =\\frac{1}{27} \\\\ {3}^{x} & =\\frac{1}{{3}^{3}} \\\\ {3}^{x} & ={3}^{-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since both sides of the equation share the same base $(3)$, we equate the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{x} & ={3}^{-3} \\\\ x & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186067318 :answer-field/correct "answer-4ff56c93-8f4d-5dca-8f7e-6a6a25c4cfda" :answer-field/choices ["answer-21ce9c20-f571-545e-977f-4d515aced9be" "answer-4ff56c93-8f4d-5dca-8f7e-6a6a25c4cfda" "answer-1903a828-2ddb-5f00-80c5-19f5e92b453a" "answer-8994455b-f891-57f8-b13b-45d1a9aa4e96" "answer-15f20d2e-d455-5504-916c-4a9743e14795"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21ce9c20-f571-545e-977f-4d515aced9be" :answer/id #uuid "21ce9c20-f571-545e-977f-4d515aced9be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ff56c93-8f4d-5dca-8f7e-6a6a25c4cfda" :answer/id #uuid "4ff56c93-8f4d-5dca-8f7e-6a6a25c4cfda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1903a828-2ddb-5f00-80c5-19f5e92b453a" :answer/id #uuid "1903a828-2ddb-5f00-80c5-19f5e92b453a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8994455b-f891-57f8-b13b-45d1a9aa4e96" :answer/id #uuid "8994455b-f891-57f8-b13b-45d1a9aa4e96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15f20d2e-d455-5504-916c-4a9743e14795" :answer/id #uuid "15f20d2e-d455-5504-916c-4a9743e14795" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179639 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ea72a94a-bdd5-5d3c-b2b4-c2e3488df948"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ea72a94a-bdd5-5d3c-b2b4-c2e3488df948" :question/id #uuid "ea72a94a-bdd5-5d3c-b2b4-c2e3488df948" :question/math-academy-id "q-208694" :question/problem "If $2mn+m+4=7,$ then $m=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We need to isolate all terms with $m$ on one side of the equation. To do this, we subtract $4$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2mn+m+4 & =7 \\\\ 2mn+m+4-4 & =7-4 \\\\ 2mn+m & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor out $m$ in the expression on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2mn+m & =3 \\\\ m(2n+1) & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides by $(2n+1)$ to isolate $m:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m(2n+1) & =3 \\\\ \\frac{m(2n+1)}{2n+1} & =\\frac{3}{2n+1} \\\\ \\frac{m\\cancel{(2n+1)}}{\\cancel{2n+1}} & =\\frac{3}{2n+1} \\\\ m & =\\frac{3}{2n+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** This result assumes that $2n+1\\ne 0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a2a58eb4-92a4-5719-9dfb-a3aad6a40bc0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a2a58eb4-92a4-5719-9dfb-a3aad6a40bc0" :answer-field/id #uuid "a2a58eb4-92a4-5719-9dfb-a3aad6a40bc0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-25c699cc-f84c-5b48-8508-432e14803537" :answer-field/choices ["answer-25c699cc-f84c-5b48-8508-432e14803537"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25c699cc-f84c-5b48-8508-432e14803537" :answer/id #uuid "25c699cc-f84c-5b48-8508-432e14803537" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2n+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068848 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-af2a1028-5c68-5261-af13-01fa26bc76aa"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-af2a1028-5c68-5261-af13-01fa26bc76aa" :question/id #uuid "af2a1028-5c68-5261-af13-01fa26bc76aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-2765" :question/problem "Factor the expression $4{r}^{2}+16r+16.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that all of the terms have a common factor of $4.$ Therefore, we can simplify the expression by factoring out $4,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{r}^{2}+16r+16 & = \\\\ 4({r}^{2}+4r+4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's factor the expression inside parentheses using the square of a sum formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{2}+4r+4 & = \\\\ {r}^{2}+4r+{2}^{2} & = \\\\ {r}^{2}+2\\cdot 2r+{2}^{2} & = \\\\ (r+2)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our original expression factors as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4({r}^{2}+4r+4) & = \\\\ 4(r+2)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3f628070-e478-5242-8b4f-a4dea04f863c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3f628070-e478-5242-8b4f-a4dea04f863c" :answer-field/id #uuid "3f628070-e478-5242-8b4f-a4dea04f863c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1b2fe58c-5054-5bba-9320-f36184ca121e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b857f724-d721-59f2-a1ef-b1e614faeab1" "answer-443effa8-8bc4-55af-875b-6cb18f9954c6" "answer-81b04f59-9424-5ce4-9b14-2e06ca51be24" "answer-1b2fe58c-5054-5bba-9320-f36184ca121e" "answer-21357de3-9850-5489-b2a4-8b42a3cf8c41"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b857f724-d721-59f2-a1ef-b1e614faeab1" :answer/id #uuid "b857f724-d721-59f2-a1ef-b1e614faeab1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2r+1)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-443effa8-8bc4-55af-875b-6cb18f9954c6" :answer/id #uuid "443effa8-8bc4-55af-875b-6cb18f9954c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2r+2)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81b04f59-9424-5ce4-9b14-2e06ca51be24" :answer/id #uuid "81b04f59-9424-5ce4-9b14-2e06ca51be24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(r+2)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b2fe58c-5054-5bba-9320-f36184ca121e" :answer/id #uuid "1b2fe58c-5054-5bba-9320-f36184ca121e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4(r+2)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21357de3-9850-5489-b2a4-8b42a3cf8c41" :answer/id #uuid "21357de3-9850-5489-b2a4-8b42a3cf8c41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4(r-2)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192636 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e2cc5506-dc0b-5a5b-8907-9924a3a993c1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e2cc5506-dc0b-5a5b-8907-9924a3a993c1" :question/id #uuid "e2cc5506-dc0b-5a5b-8907-9924a3a993c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-215510" :question/problem "Written in ascending order, the solutions to $|1-2x|-2=7$ are $x=${{field-1}}\nand $x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the absolute value on the left side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|1-2x|-2 & =7 \\\\ |1-2x| & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following two cases:\n\n- If $|1-2x|=1-2x,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|1-2x| & =9 \\\\ 1-2x & =9 \\\\ -2x & =8 \\\\ x & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|1-2x|=-(1-2x),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|1-2x| & =9 \\\\ -(1-2x) & =9 \\\\ -1+2x & =9 \\\\ 2x & =10 \\\\ x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-4$ and $x=5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4805b999-73a4-56f9-85d1-fd39b746b678" "answer-field-551c716c-7245-54c5-b067-9d77aa114b1a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4805b999-73a4-56f9-85d1-fd39b746b678" :answer-field/id #uuid "4805b999-73a4-56f9-85d1-fd39b746b678" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-dad0e77a-e20e-537d-a75c-ebf6a272d4ad" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dad0e77a-e20e-537d-a75c-ebf6a272d4ad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dad0e77a-e20e-537d-a75c-ebf6a272d4ad" :answer/id #uuid "dad0e77a-e20e-537d-a75c-ebf6a272d4ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-551c716c-7245-54c5-b067-9d77aa114b1a" :answer-field/id #uuid "551c716c-7245-54c5-b067-9d77aa114b1a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-92345246-b68e-50d2-85cc-0c9a1ffea68e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-92345246-b68e-50d2-85cc-0c9a1ffea68e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92345246-b68e-50d2-85cc-0c9a1ffea68e" :answer/id #uuid "92345246-b68e-50d2-85cc-0c9a1ffea68e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186069424 :question/problem "Simplify $\\sqrt[3]{-\\frac{64}{{b}^{3}}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To simplify the expression, we write the term under the radical as a perfect cube, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{-\\frac{64}{{b}^{3}}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{(-\\frac{4}{b})\\cdot (-\\frac{4}{b})\\cdot (-\\frac{4}{b})} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{(-\\frac{4}{b})}^{3}} & = \\\\ -\\frac{4}{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186067714 :answer-field/correct 17592186067715 :answer-field/choices ["answer-b1595b53-a21f-533f-948c-76530eaa78e7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1595b53-a21f-533f-948c-76530eaa78e7" :answer/id #uuid "b1595b53-a21f-533f-948c-76530eaa78e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{{b}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115408 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f2983b81-0133-59cc-8912-96155bb43215"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f2983b81-0133-59cc-8912-96155bb43215" :question/id #uuid "f2983b81-0133-59cc-8912-96155bb43215" :question/math-academy-id "q-117951" :question/problem "![](images/30/304c79983ae3d5cdc007d62aa8e30bac247c1370239a9029a33b21b7fcf2f309.png)\n\nOrder the sides of the triangle $△RST$ above from the shortest to the longest." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the missing angle $T.$ Since the interior angles of a triangle sum to ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠R+m∠S+m∠T & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ {40}^{∘}+{103}^{∘}+m∠T & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠T & ={180}^{∘}-{143}^{∘} \\\\ m∠T & ={37}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $∠T$ is the smallest angle, its opposite side $\\overset{―}{RS}$ is the shortest side of the triangle.\n\nSince $∠S$ is the largest angle, its opposite side $\\overset{―}{RT}$ must be the longest side of the triangle. \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nRS<ST<RT\n$$\n\nand therefore, the required order is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{RS},\\overset{―}{ST},\\overset{―}{RT}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1d7a78bb-16be-5300-81b5-d88dcf737ba7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1d7a78bb-16be-5300-81b5-d88dcf737ba7" :answer-field/id #uuid "1d7a78bb-16be-5300-81b5-d88dcf737ba7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cb6c7bae-6800-5585-892f-162cfd43f379" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6c64bbe2-dc8b-59c6-8ea8-95bb9a823367" "answer-cb6c7bae-6800-5585-892f-162cfd43f379" "answer-201ce639-d825-59d4-909d-cc029b989d10" "answer-bee89c04-7119-59e0-b530-75c0a845b5fd" "answer-f5e1a852-120a-5338-ab79-edc1563e6cf1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c64bbe2-dc8b-59c6-8ea8-95bb9a823367" :answer/id #uuid "6c64bbe2-dc8b-59c6-8ea8-95bb9a823367" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{―}{RS},\\overset{―}{RT},\\overset{―}{ST}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb6c7bae-6800-5585-892f-162cfd43f379" :answer/id #uuid "cb6c7bae-6800-5585-892f-162cfd43f379" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{―}{RS},\\overset{―}{ST},\\overset{―}{RT}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-201ce639-d825-59d4-909d-cc029b989d10" :answer/id #uuid "201ce639-d825-59d4-909d-cc029b989d10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{―}{RT},\\overset{―}{RS},\\overset{―}{ST}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bee89c04-7119-59e0-b530-75c0a845b5fd" :answer/id #uuid "bee89c04-7119-59e0-b530-75c0a845b5fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{―}{RT},\\overset{―}{ST},\\overset{―}{RS}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5e1a852-120a-5338-ab79-edc1563e6cf1" :answer/id #uuid "f5e1a852-120a-5338-ab79-edc1563e6cf1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{―}{ST},\\overset{―}{RS},\\overset{―}{RT}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054770 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5c6ca484-3f17-5181-8810-930cfb1991ba"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5c6ca484-3f17-5181-8810-930cfb1991ba" :question/id #uuid "5c6ca484-3f17-5181-8810-930cfb1991ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-171612" :question/problem "The solution to the inequality $-2a\\ge 10$ is $a${{field-1}}{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The variable $a$ is being *multiplied* by $-2.$ To isolate $a,$ we perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $-2.$ Remember to perform the same operation on both sides.\n\nAlso, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2a\\,\\, & \\ge \\,\\,10 \\\\ \\frac{-2a}{-2}\\,\\, & \\le \\,\\,\\frac{10}{-2} \\\\ \\frac{-2a}{-2}\\,\\, & \\le \\,\\,-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $-2$ from both the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-2a}{-2} & \\le -5 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-2}a}{\\cancel{-2}} & \\le -5 \\\\ a & \\le -5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $a\\le -5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ac508ebb-eb69-5e10-b789-82b08fb0c3a2" "answer-field-217bc00d-ea7b-5b67-b963-3c6eb56a93da"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ac508ebb-eb69-5e10-b789-82b08fb0c3a2" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac508ebb-eb69-5e10-b789-82b08fb0c3a2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-5b908877-4e9b-5192-8fd2-65f4fa1e3b4e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5b908877-4e9b-5192-8fd2-65f4fa1e3b4e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b908877-4e9b-5192-8fd2-65f4fa1e3b4e" :answer/id #uuid "5b908877-4e9b-5192-8fd2-65f4fa1e3b4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\le" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-217bc00d-ea7b-5b67-b963-3c6eb56a93da" :answer-field/id #uuid "217bc00d-ea7b-5b67-b963-3c6eb56a93da" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-a8eccfa2-7023-5398-8b0c-e3113e038df8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a8eccfa2-7023-5398-8b0c-e3113e038df8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8eccfa2-7023-5398-8b0c-e3113e038df8" :answer/id #uuid "a8eccfa2-7023-5398-8b0c-e3113e038df8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078531 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fe6f82c7-c73d-5fb8-9cbc-ff242831dba6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-fe6f82c7-c73d-5fb8-9cbc-ff242831dba6" :question/id #uuid "fe6f82c7-c73d-5fb8-9cbc-ff242831dba6" :question/math-academy-id "q-44680" :question/problem "Evaluate the polynomial $\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{3z}{4}-\\frac{1}{2}$ at $z=2.$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate, we substitute $z=2$  into the polynomial and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{3z}{4}-\\frac{1}{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{{2}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{3(2)}{4}-\\frac{1}{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{4}{4}+\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} & = \\\\ 1+1 & = \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-15720162-78da-5cb1-b598-b8344581476a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-15720162-78da-5cb1-b598-b8344581476a" :answer-field/id #uuid "15720162-78da-5cb1-b598-b8344581476a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2354abcc-cea2-5f54-b025-a493d7f2f10e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-677f5fec-7b47-57ac-aa80-a11d479550ef" "answer-2354abcc-cea2-5f54-b025-a493d7f2f10e" "answer-8825f5d3-ef9c-51d5-9ac8-54ce1710ff19" "answer-f79a8362-7b0c-58c0-a434-d4d47dde22c4" "answer-4b2e51f9-9a04-5a20-a5d2-ec9135740a69"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-677f5fec-7b47-57ac-aa80-a11d479550ef" :answer/id #uuid "677f5fec-7b47-57ac-aa80-a11d479550ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2354abcc-cea2-5f54-b025-a493d7f2f10e" :answer/id #uuid "2354abcc-cea2-5f54-b025-a493d7f2f10e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8825f5d3-ef9c-51d5-9ac8-54ce1710ff19" :answer/id #uuid "8825f5d3-ef9c-51d5-9ac8-54ce1710ff19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f79a8362-7b0c-58c0-a434-d4d47dde22c4" :answer/id #uuid "f79a8362-7b0c-58c0-a434-d4d47dde22c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b2e51f9-9a04-5a20-a5d2-ec9135740a69" :answer/id #uuid "4b2e51f9-9a04-5a20-a5d2-ec9135740a69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176098 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-47312f69-f326-5376-9041-14157a2dd5a5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-47312f69-f326-5376-9041-14157a2dd5a5" :question/id #uuid "47312f69-f326-5376-9041-14157a2dd5a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-103266" :question/problem "![](images/4f/4f538bb715c53ad0478539feaef29c725f6f6e494134726faede38586e60a4d6.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the angles shown above?\n\nI. $m∠AOB=m∠BOC$\n\nII. $m∠BOC=m∠COD$\n\nIII. $∠AOB≅∠DOE$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that \n\n- $∠AOB$ and $∠BOC$ are marked with $|$, and\n\n- $∠COD$ and $∠DOE$ are marked with $||.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∠AOB & ≅∠BOC \\\\ ∠COD & ≅∠DOE.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOB & =m∠BOC \\\\ m∠COD & =m∠DOE.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo statement I is true, while statements II and III are false." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6452e741-3219-5674-aa9c-11f468eb9f0b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6452e741-3219-5674-aa9c-11f468eb9f0b" :answer-field/id #uuid "6452e741-3219-5674-aa9c-11f468eb9f0b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1d40922e-bbe8-5b94-813f-515ef8920c77" :answer-field/choices ["answer-71b862ff-f819-58ba-8500-e7a6c8b9b38e" "answer-1d40922e-bbe8-5b94-813f-515ef8920c77" "answer-99bd640f-26eb-57be-b433-3a9313b2d3bf" "answer-f212cd6f-41a2-599e-83ee-e2b7414a0f6a" "answer-46af0f5c-e63b-5c43-8a7a-63eca133b229"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-71b862ff-f819-58ba-8500-e7a6c8b9b38e" :answer/id #uuid "71b862ff-f819-58ba-8500-e7a6c8b9b38e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d40922e-bbe8-5b94-813f-515ef8920c77" :answer/id #uuid "1d40922e-bbe8-5b94-813f-515ef8920c77" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99bd640f-26eb-57be-b433-3a9313b2d3bf" :answer/id #uuid "99bd640f-26eb-57be-b433-3a9313b2d3bf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f212cd6f-41a2-599e-83ee-e2b7414a0f6a" :answer/id #uuid "f212cd6f-41a2-599e-83ee-e2b7414a0f6a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46af0f5c-e63b-5c43-8a7a-63eca133b229" :answer/id #uuid "46af0f5c-e63b-5c43-8a7a-63eca133b229" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186074001 :question/problem "$4\\sqrt{3}-5\\sqrt{12}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we use the product rule for radicals, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{12} & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 3}=\\sqrt{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}=2\\sqrt{3} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\sqrt{3}-5\\sqrt{12} & = \\\\ 4\\sqrt{3}-5(2\\sqrt{3}) & = \\\\ 4\\sqrt{3}-10\\sqrt{3}. & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can combine the two $\\sqrt{3}$ terms together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\sqrt{3}-10\\sqrt{3} & = \\\\ (4-10)\\sqrt{3} & = \\\\ -6\\sqrt{3} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186070091 :answer-field/correct 17592186070094 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110617 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c20addaa-2ef3-5691-8ace-1f1d2895fe58"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c20addaa-2ef3-5691-8ace-1f1d2895fe58" :question/id #uuid "c20addaa-2ef3-5691-8ace-1f1d2895fe58" :question/math-academy-id "q-68963" :question/problem "${({5}^{3}\\times 3)}^{4}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the power of product rule for exponents:\n\n$$\n{({5}^{3}\\times 3)}^{4}={({5}^{3})}^{4}\\times {3}^{4}\n$$\n\nThen, we rewrite the first factor using the power rule for exponents, and simplify:\n\n$$\n{({5}^{3})}^{4}\\times {3}^{4}={5}^{3\\cdot 4}\\times {3}^{4}={5}^{12}\\times {3}^{4}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8bd771f8-1da2-5ff5-b018-e0a61817e437"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8bd771f8-1da2-5ff5-b018-e0a61817e437" :answer-field/id #uuid "8bd771f8-1da2-5ff5-b018-e0a61817e437" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-505fc778-325e-5f2c-b027-1e6623d55f37" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7612e3e8-6c41-58cd-b9cd-de345315c958" "answer-505fc778-325e-5f2c-b027-1e6623d55f37" "answer-f8652722-ecb3-51f0-bc15-77dae7eb9a77" "answer-e38221f4-6a33-5206-9b11-ccf256f3aa86" "answer-0ac94868-df19-5ec5-bcd2-c6a2c7a548b7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7612e3e8-6c41-58cd-b9cd-de345315c958" :answer/id #uuid "7612e3e8-6c41-58cd-b9cd-de345315c958" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{5}^{10}\\times {3}^{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-505fc778-325e-5f2c-b027-1e6623d55f37" :answer/id #uuid "505fc778-325e-5f2c-b027-1e6623d55f37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{5}^{12}\\times {3}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f8652722-ecb3-51f0-bc15-77dae7eb9a77" :answer/id #uuid "f8652722-ecb3-51f0-bc15-77dae7eb9a77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{5}^{12}\\times {3}^{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e38221f4-6a33-5206-9b11-ccf256f3aa86" :answer/id #uuid "e38221f4-6a33-5206-9b11-ccf256f3aa86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{5}^{3}\\times {3}^{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ac94868-df19-5ec5-bcd2-c6a2c7a548b7" :answer/id #uuid "0ac94868-df19-5ec5-bcd2-c6a2c7a548b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{5}^{7}\\times {3}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064194 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2c796978-9336-5fc7-a4cc-bd1fe1ccd4cd"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2c796978-9336-5fc7-a4cc-bd1fe1ccd4cd" :question/id #uuid "2c796978-9336-5fc7-a4cc-bd1fe1ccd4cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-215096" :question/problem "If $v=2τdh,$ then $τ=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We need to isolate $τ,$ so we will treat the other variables $v,d,$ and $h$ as constants. We can use the multiplication principle to solve for $τ.$\n\nFirst, we rearrange and then divide both sides by $2dh:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =2τdh \\\\ v & =(2dh)τ \\\\ \\frac{v}{2dh} & =\\frac{(2dh)τ}{2dh} \\\\ \\frac{v}{2dh} & =τ\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $τ=\\frac{v}{2dh}.$\n\n**Note:** This result assumes that $d\\ne 0$ and $h\\ne 0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-066b2166-822f-5d65-8ee3-2f1f64ae2d7d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-066b2166-822f-5d65-8ee3-2f1f64ae2d7d" :answer-field/id #uuid "066b2166-822f-5d65-8ee3-2f1f64ae2d7d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-71a54dfc-a7bc-50b1-888f-91e3d09fe8d3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-71a54dfc-a7bc-50b1-888f-91e3d09fe8d3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-71a54dfc-a7bc-50b1-888f-91e3d09fe8d3" :answer/id #uuid "71a54dfc-a7bc-50b1-888f-91e3d09fe8d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{v}{2dh}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133921 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d9b9c93d-9a95-57ab-bfc8-b62b1c153ff8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d9b9c93d-9a95-57ab-bfc8-b62b1c153ff8" :question/id #uuid "d9b9c93d-9a95-57ab-bfc8-b62b1c153ff8" :question/math-academy-id "q-63877" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\sqrt[3]{5y+1}$ at $y=3.$" :question/worked-solution "We replace $y$ with $3$ in the given expression, and simplify as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{5y+1} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{5\\cdot 3+1} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{15+1} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{16} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{8\\cdot 2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{8}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{2}^{3}}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{2} & = \\\\ 2\\sqrt[3]{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b9a3fd1a-2273-5c72-90b6-7e74178421d4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b9a3fd1a-2273-5c72-90b6-7e74178421d4" :answer-field/id #uuid "b9a3fd1a-2273-5c72-90b6-7e74178421d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3af63541-1762-58f0-a991-4c6b26b43531" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3af63541-1762-58f0-a991-4c6b26b43531" "answer-b93ea9d0-8b76-54b8-8b51-d66c68f7b7fd" "answer-bba12de4-ce73-58e0-91af-1d1824b8de14" "answer-27fdf04b-368f-516d-9e0e-8cca33d47e26" "answer-69a0d827-e260-5878-81a5-f3ff4aab7335"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3af63541-1762-58f0-a991-4c6b26b43531" :answer/id #uuid "3af63541-1762-58f0-a991-4c6b26b43531" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt[3]{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b93ea9d0-8b7