520855-d5ff-5b95-a240-bee4bebe295a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c9c2a68b-e255-5fdf-85ea-2c83a681b9e6" :answer-field/id #uuid "c9c2a68b-e255-5fdf-85ea-2c83a681b9e6" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e043e72b-6724-5f64-a1b4-a804419a914e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e043e72b-6724-5f64-a1b4-a804419a914e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e043e72b-6724-5f64-a1b4-a804419a914e" :answer/id #uuid "e043e72b-6724-5f64-a1b4-a804419a914e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f7c9306b-afe2-5131-b1e8-c49c5134ad1f" :answer-field/id #uuid "f7c9306b-afe2-5131-b1e8-c49c5134ad1f" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-0f8bfe3c-c586-586c-87cb-39aabb55a3fe" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0f8bfe3c-c586-586c-87cb-39aabb55a3fe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f8bfe3c-c586-586c-87cb-39aabb55a3fe" :answer/id #uuid "0f8bfe3c-c586-586c-87cb-39aabb55a3fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1bfb5188-7c59-596d-bb0b-41e90d79e407" :question/id #uuid "1bfb5188-7c59-596d-bb0b-41e90d79e407" :question/math-academy-id "q-355247" :question/problem "| $t$ | $h(t)$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-5$ | $4$ |\n| $-2$ | $-1$ |\n| $3$ | $7$ |\n| $6$ | $-6$ |\n\nThe table above gives values of a function $h$ on the set $T=\\{-5,-2,3,6\\}.$ Compute the following:\n\n${max}_{t\\in T}h(t)=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{t\\in T}h(t)=$\n{{field-2}}\n\n${min}_{t\\in T}h(t)=$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{t\\in T}h(t)=$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n- ${max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the maximum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that maximum output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- ${min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the minimum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that minimum output occurs.\n\nThe output values are $4,-1,7,$ and $-6.$ The maximum output is $7$ (at $t=3$), and the minimum output is $-6$ (at $t=6$). \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{max}_{t\\in T}h(t) & =7 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{t\\in T}h(t) & =3 \\\\ {min}_{t\\in T}h(t) & =-6 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{t\\in T}h(t) & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-14091760-d318-52ef-8f7a-1e7f1505bba7" "answer-field-ecf45cf3-40ef-52e7-9ec6-57d10541f220" "answer-field-9336c99c-17c3-5144-b0dc-5fdffe1c6c29" "answer-field-454cc990-2c69-5f82-8f07-4ebe88482891"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-14091760-d318-52ef-8f7a-1e7f1505bba7" :answer-field/id #uuid "14091760-d318-52ef-8f7a-1e7f1505bba7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-876868ab-7914-5326-9f9e-f52520e3fd18" :answer-field/choices ["answer-876868ab-7914-5326-9f9e-f52520e3fd18"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-876868ab-7914-5326-9f9e-f52520e3fd18" :answer/id #uuid "876868ab-7914-5326-9f9e-f52520e3fd18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ecf45cf3-40ef-52e7-9ec6-57d10541f220" :answer-field/id #uuid "ecf45cf3-40ef-52e7-9ec6-57d10541f220" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-bad574c3-61ab-5018-b7c2-e81c899ee288" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bad574c3-61ab-5018-b7c2-e81c899ee288"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bad574c3-61ab-5018-b7c2-e81c899ee288" :answer/id #uuid "bad574c3-61ab-5018-b7c2-e81c899ee288" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9336c99c-17c3-5144-b0dc-5fdffe1c6c29" :answer-field/id #uuid "9336c99c-17c3-5144-b0dc-5fdffe1c6c29" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-29f448ec-e2f7-5423-9c43-b27c85d08ed7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-29f448ec-e2f7-5423-9c43-b27c85d08ed7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29f448ec-e2f7-5423-9c43-b27c85d08ed7" :answer/id #uuid "29f448ec-e2f7-5423-9c43-b27c85d08ed7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-454cc990-2c69-5f82-8f07-4ebe88482891" :answer-field/id #uuid "454cc990-2c69-5f82-8f07-4ebe88482891" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-444d695f-eab4-54fb-aadd-bba536c6e35e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-444d695f-eab4-54fb-aadd-bba536c6e35e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-444d695f-eab4-54fb-aadd-bba536c6e35e" :answer/id #uuid "444d695f-eab4-54fb-aadd-bba536c6e35e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-e91f729f-e72b-5ce9-ba10-21e7bc94ffcc" :activity/id #uuid "e91f729f-e72b-5ce9-ba10-21e7bc94ffcc" :activity/title "Finding Argmax and Argmin From Tables and Graphs" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186051002 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-3d5d27c0-3347-5be2-804c-f52fe79f2580" "step-91db8244-3685-5e70-84f7-d0eb181b472e" "step-d987c069-950d-51ec-b40d-d6b2adce6a4e" "step-38507fa3-e58a-5d15-9bed-68d9c6b28a9f" "step-475846c9-31fa-598e-958f-494404cc26b8"] :activity/first-step "step-3d5d27c0-3347-5be2-804c-f52fe79f2580" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-3d5d27c0-3347-5be2-804c-f52fe79f2580" :step/id #uuid "3d5d27c0-3347-5be2-804c-f52fe79f2580" :step/content 17592186231738 :step/next "step-91db8244-3685-5e70-84f7-d0eb181b472e" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-91db8244-3685-5e70-84f7-d0eb181b472e" :step/id #uuid "91db8244-3685-5e70-84f7-d0eb181b472e" :step/content "question-872e3e1c-801d-5da3-9c5c-97c11a673f6e" :step/next "step-d987c069-950d-51ec-b40d-d6b2adce6a4e" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d987c069-950d-51ec-b40d-d6b2adce6a4e" :step/id #uuid "d987c069-950d-51ec-b40d-d6b2adce6a4e" :step/content "question-c6c0cc6c-d71f-5404-a9ca-d9e5fa0bb209" :step/next "step-38507fa3-e58a-5d15-9bed-68d9c6b28a9f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-38507fa3-e58a-5d15-9bed-68d9c6b28a9f" :step/id #uuid "38507fa3-e58a-5d15-9bed-68d9c6b28a9f" :step/content "question-aa3208c3-dd8f-52a7-9e52-31f81d41b1b4" :step/next "step-475846c9-31fa-598e-958f-494404cc26b8" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-475846c9-31fa-598e-958f-494404cc26b8" :step/id #uuid "475846c9-31fa-598e-958f-494404cc26b8" :step/content "question-1bfb5188-7c59-596d-bb0b-41e90d79e407" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166847 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9c281bbc-e5bb-5c0b-9b81-0eabf770ee2e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9c281bbc-e5bb-5c0b-9b81-0eabf770ee2e" :question/id #uuid "9c281bbc-e5bb-5c0b-9b81-0eabf770ee2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-147885" :question/problem "The disjoint union ${A}_{1}⊔{A}_{2}⊔{A}_{3}⊔{A}_{4}$ of events ${A}_{1},{A}_{2},{A}_{3},{A}_{4}$ covers the entire sample space. Compute $P({A}_{2}|B)$ given the following probabilities:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & P(B|{A}_{1})=0.25, & P({A}_{1})=0.28 \\\\  & P(B|{A}_{2})=0.3, &  \\\\  & P(B|{A}_{3})=0.28, & P({A}_{3})=0.18 \\\\  & P(B|{A}_{4})=0.1, & P({A}_{4})=0.22\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRound your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "If the disjoint union ${A}_{1}⊔{A}_{2}⊔…⊔{A}_{n}$ covers the entire sample space, Bayes' theorem combined with the law of total probability gives us the following:\n\n$$\nP({A}_{k}|B)=\\frac{P(B|{A}_{k})P({A}_{k})}{P(B)}=\\frac{P(B|{A}_{k})P({A}_{k})}{{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}P(B|{A}_{i})P({A}_{i})}\n$$\n\nwhere $k=1,2,…,n.$\n\nIn our case, $n=4,$ and ${A}_{1}⊔{A}_{2}⊔{A}_{3}⊔{A}_{4}$ covers the entire sample space. Consequently, we have\n\n$$\nP({A}_{1})+P({A}_{2})+P({A}_{3})+P({A}_{4})=1.\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({A}_{2}) & =1-(P({A}_{1})+P({A}_{3})+P({A}_{4})) \\\\  & =1-(0.28+0.18+0.22) \\\\  & =0.32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({A}_{2}|B) & =\\frac{P(B|{A}_{2})P({A}_{2})}{{\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}P(B|{A}_{i})P({A}_{i})} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(B|{A}_{2})P({A}_{2})}{P(B|{A}_{1})P({A}_{1})+P(B|{A}_{2})P({A}_{2})+P(B|{A}_{3})P({A}_{3})+P(B|{A}_{4})P({A}_{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.3)(0.32)}{(0.25)(0.28)+(0.3)(0.32)+(0.28)(0.18)+(0.1)(0.22)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.096}{0.2384} \\\\  & ≈0.403.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-266b7c98-bb0c-5250-98ae-54d840c489c2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-266b7c98-bb0c-5250-98ae-54d840c489c2" :answer-field/id #uuid "266b7c98-bb0c-5250-98ae-54d840c489c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cb1644a5-6db3-535c-a833-2c384185599d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3abf36e3-3cf2-5339-8e78-9d57d7acb48a" "answer-408cef73-e79b-5f84-909b-bb78b0af2709" "answer-161fb25c-96cf-5b02-8d7d-25af5ca8f28a" "answer-cb1644a5-6db3-535c-a833-2c384185599d" "answer-c7987182-3703-5340-83e1-52554f33e28f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3abf36e3-3cf2-5339-8e78-9d57d7acb48a" :answer/id #uuid "3abf36e3-3cf2-5339-8e78-9d57d7acb48a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.286" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-408cef73-e79b-5f84-909b-bb78b0af2709" :answer/id #uuid "408cef73-e79b-5f84-909b-bb78b0af2709" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.322" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-161fb25c-96cf-5b02-8d7d-25af5ca8f28a" :answer/id #uuid "161fb25c-96cf-5b02-8d7d-25af5ca8f28a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.365" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb1644a5-6db3-535c-a833-2c384185599d" :answer/id #uuid "cb1644a5-6db3-535c-a833-2c384185599d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.403" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7987182-3703-5340-83e1-52554f33e28f" :answer/id #uuid "c7987182-3703-5340-83e1-52554f33e28f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.444" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166877 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-095773d5-faca-5dcc-94ed-85e3db151ccc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-095773d5-faca-5dcc-94ed-85e3db151ccc" :question/id #uuid "095773d5-faca-5dcc-94ed-85e3db151ccc" :question/math-academy-id "q-148082" :question/problem "A medical center is investigating the correlation between scoliosis and sports practice in a sample of children.\n\n- $25%$ of children in the sample don't practice sports, and $3%$ of those children have scoliosis.\n\n- $30%$ of children in the sample practice one sport, and $2.5%$ of those children have scoliosis.\n\n- $45%$ of children in the sample practice two sports, and $3.3%$ of those children have scoliosis.\n\nIf $52%$ of children in the entire sample are female, and $2%$ of female children have scoliosis, what is the probability that a randomly chosen child with scoliosis is female? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let $F$ be the event that a child is female, $C$ be the event that a child has scoliosis, and ${S}_{0},{S}_{1},{S}_{2}$ be the event that a child practice $0,$ $1,$ or $2$ sports, respectively.\n\nLet's break down the information given in the problem statement:\n\n- From the bullet points, we have the following information:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & P({S}_{0})=0.25 &  & P(C|{S}_{0})=0.03 \\\\  & P({S}_{1})=0.30 &  & P(C|{S}_{1})=0.025 \\\\  & P({S}_{2})=0.45 &  & P(C|{S}_{2})=0.033\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe disjoint union ${S}_{0}⊔{S}_{1}⊔{S}_{2}$ covers the entire sample space, and we have\n\n$$\nP({S}_{0})+P({S}_{1})+P({S}_{2})=0.25+0.30+0.45=1.\n$$\n\n- Since $52%$ of children in the entire sample are female, we have\n\n$$\nP(F)=0.52.\n$$\n\n- Since $2%$ of females have scoliosis, we have\n\n$$\nP(C|F)=0.02.\n$$\n\nWe want to find the probability that a randomly chosen child with scoliosis is female, which is represented as $P(F|C).$ \n\nUsing Bayes' theorem combined with the law of total probability, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(F|C) & =\\frac{P(C|F)P(F)}{P(C)} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(C|F)P(F)}{P(C|{S}_{0})P({S}_{0})+P(C|{S}_{1})P({S}_{1})+P(C|{S}_{2})P({S}_{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.02)(0.52)}{(0.03)(0.25)+(0.025)(0.3)+(0.033)(0.45)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.0104}{0.0299} \\\\  & ≈0.348,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-af85ec6e-7016-53c3-802c-9198ac759320"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-af85ec6e-7016-53c3-802c-9198ac759320" :answer-field/id #uuid "af85ec6e-7016-53c3-802c-9198ac759320" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-144c9c56-d288-5656-9e9a-114c97ea9460" :answer-field/choices ["answer-144c9c56-d288-5656-9e9a-114c97ea9460" "answer-39018054-1073-5cec-87c0-3be506864193" "answer-7aae2ee8-a81d-50e2-98ea-e2df978f83a9" "answer-85700ac7-cad1-590c-a143-b418ccc70b5b" "answer-7dd4d43d-b30b-5f97-8032-3941bf17d1fb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-144c9c56-d288-5656-9e9a-114c97ea9460" :answer/id #uuid "144c9c56-d288-5656-9e9a-114c97ea9460" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.348" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39018054-1073-5cec-87c0-3be506864193" :answer/id #uuid "39018054-1073-5cec-87c0-3be506864193" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.415" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7aae2ee8-a81d-50e2-98ea-e2df978f83a9" :answer/id #uuid "7aae2ee8-a81d-50e2-98ea-e2df978f83a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-85700ac7-cad1-590c-a143-b418ccc70b5b" :answer/id #uuid "85700ac7-cad1-590c-a143-b418ccc70b5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.52" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7dd4d43d-b30b-5f97-8032-3941bf17d1fb" :answer/id #uuid "7dd4d43d-b30b-5f97-8032-3941bf17d1fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.552" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166848 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1787d264-9d95-57d2-8330-7eec4c052cfe"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-1787d264-9d95-57d2-8330-7eec4c052cfe" :question/id #uuid "1787d264-9d95-57d2-8330-7eec4c052cfe" :question/math-academy-id "q-148271" :question/problem "A medical center is investigating the correlation between scoliosis and sports practice in a sample of children.\n\n- $25%$ of children in the sample don't practice sports, and $2.5%$ of those children have scoliosis.\n\n- $30%$ of children in the sample practice one sport.\n\n- $45%$ of children in the sample practice two sports, and $2.8%$ of those children have scoliosis.\n\nIf $48%$ of children in the entire sample are female, $2.6%$ of female children have scoliosis, and $46%$ of children with scoliosis are female, what is the probability that a randomly chosen child who practices one sport has scoliosis? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let $F$ be the event that a child is female, $C$ be the event that a child has scoliosis, and ${S}_{0},{S}_{1},{S}_{2}$ be the event that a child practices $0,$ $1,$ or $2$ sports, respectively.\n\nLet's break down the information given in the problem statement:\n\n- From the bullet points, we have the following information:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & P({S}_{0})=0.25 &  & P(C∣{S}_{0})=0.025 \\\\  & P({S}_{1})=0.30 \\\\  & P({S}_{2})=0.45 &  & P(C∣{S}_{2})=0.028\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe disjoint union ${S}_{0}⊔{S}_{1}⊔{S}_{2}$ covers the entire sample space, and we have\n\n$$\nP({S}_{0})+P({S}_{1})+P({S}_{2})=0.25+0.30+0.45=1.\n$$\n\n- Since $48%$ of students in the entire sample are female, we have\n\n$$\nP(F)=0.48.\n$$\n\n- Since $2.6%$ of females have scoliosis, we have\n\n$$\nP(C∣F)=0.026.\n$$\n\n- Since $46%$ of children with scoliosis are female, we have\n\n$$\nP(F∣C)=0.46.\n$$\n\nWe want to find the probability that a randomly chosen child who practices one sport has scoliosis, which is represented as $P(C∣{S}_{1}).$\n\nUsing Bayes' theorem combined with the law of total probability, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(F∣C) & =\\frac{P(C∣F)P(F)}{P(C)} \\\\ P(F∣C) & =\\frac{P(C∣F)P(F)}{P(C∣{S}_{0})P({S}_{0})+P(C∣{S}_{1})P({S}_{1})+P(C∣{S}_{2})P({S}_{2})} \\\\ 0.46 & =\\frac{(0.026)(0.48)}{(0.25)(0.025)+P(C∣{S}_{1})(0.3)+(0.028)(0.45)} \\\\ 0.46 & =\\frac{0.0125}{0.0189+0.3P(C∣{S}_{1})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $P(C∣{S}_{1}),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.46(0.0189+0.3P(C∣{S}_{1})) & =0.0125 \\\\ 0.0189+0.3P(C∣{S}_{1}) & =\\frac{0.0125}{0.46} \\\\ 0.3P(C∣{S}_{1}) & =\\frac{0.0125}{0.46}-0.0189 \\\\ P(C∣{S}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{0.3}(\\frac{0.0125}{0.46}-0.0189) \\\\ P(C∣{S}_{1}) & ≈0.028\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2d9e6faf-9e8f-5d9c-aa84-79845b127ed4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2d9e6faf-9e8f-5d9c-aa84-79845b127ed4" :answer-field/id #uuid "2d9e6faf-9e8f-5d9c-aa84-79845b127ed4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c97eb869-625e-551f-be3b-c0ff2ec27876" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a2ac414e-15b9-5ce9-93e3-a7f2a6d829da" "answer-c97eb869-625e-551f-be3b-c0ff2ec27876" "answer-8a26048a-fd81-56ee-8af6-bd08ebb325b0" "answer-50e9c58b-4fb9-5497-9482-e8f285727015" "answer-5b9c5c15-f6a2-5b4a-a895-22168d05307d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2ac414e-15b9-5ce9-93e3-a7f2a6d829da" :answer/id #uuid "a2ac414e-