968" :step/id #uuid "964218e8-bf1c-559e-ad24-e50227ec5968" :step/content "question-095773d5-faca-5dcc-94ed-85e3db151ccc" :step/next "step-fce198a3-2fe3-5172-8c78-1731bf8adc70" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-fce198a3-2fe3-5172-8c78-1731bf8adc70" :step/id #uuid "fce198a3-2fe3-5172-8c78-1731bf8adc70" :step/content 17592186487402 :step/next "step-39ce452f-966f-5775-99e0-20fb8ca0eef9" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-39ce452f-966f-5775-99e0-20fb8ca0eef9" :step/id #uuid "39ce452f-966f-5775-99e0-20fb8ca0eef9" :step/content "question-1787d264-9d95-57d2-8330-7eec4c052cfe" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204081 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-078844cb-65ac-54f4-bde7-64e4bd44f313"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204583 :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{2\\times 3}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)=\\frac{1}{2}(Ax-b)^{T}(Ax-b),$ where\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${∇}_{A}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-160$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWe can compute $\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}$ by applying the chain rule.\n\nLet $y=Ax-b\\in {R}^{2}.$ Then, $L(A)=\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{T}y$ and\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}={\\sum }_{k=1}^{2}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n{∇}_{y}L={∇}_{y}(\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{T}y)=y,\n$$\n\nwe have that\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}={y}_{k}.\n$$\n\nWriting out $y=Ax-b$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\n{y}_{i}={\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}{a}_{ij}{x}_{j}-{b}_{i},\n$$\n\nwe have \n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}={x}_{j}$ if $i=k$, and\n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}=0$ if $i\\ne k.$\n\nThis means that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}} & ={\\sum }_{k=1}^{2}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{i}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & ={y}_{i}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & ={y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $(i,j)$th entry of ${∇}_{A}L$ is the $i$th entry of $y$ multiplied by the $j$th entry of $x$, so\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=y\\cdot {x}^{T}.\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating ${∇}_{A}L$ at $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{A}L & =y\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =(Ax-b)\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =([\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 10 & 20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =([\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 10 & 20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 10 & 20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 130 & 260 \\\\ 0 & -80 & -160\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203428 :answer-field/correct "answer-390d31e7-0eb4-5afa-8052-7ccdd44c6579" :answer-field/choices ["answer-390d31e7-0eb4-5afa-8052-7ccdd44c6579"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-390d31e7-0eb4-5afa-8052-7ccdd44c6579" :answer/id #uuid "390d31e7-0eb4-5afa-8052-7ccdd44c6579" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203431 :answer-field/correct "answer-e1be0ef3-af8e-50ef-8a85-884fab6e57c6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e1be0ef3-af8e-50ef-8a85-884fab6e57c6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e1be0ef3-af8e-50ef-8a85-884fab6e57c6" :answer/id #uuid "e1be0ef3-af8e-50ef-8a85-884fab6e57c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "130" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203429 :answer-field/correct "answer-4bf55f8d-69c2-5804-b198-4e612f8ef966" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4bf55f8d-69c2-5804-b198-4e612f8ef966"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4bf55f8d-69c2-5804-b198-4e612f8ef966" :answer/id #uuid "4bf55f8d-69c2-5804-b198-4e612f8ef966" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "260" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203430 :answer-field/correct "answer-d24effe3-93a6-51e3-92fb-67753603fb63" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d24effe3-93a6-51e3-92fb-67753603fb63"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d24effe3-93a6-51e3-92fb-67753603fb63" :answer/id #uuid "d24effe3-93a6-51e3-92fb-67753603fb63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-80" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204080 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7c674592-16b0-5e5a-b0ac-ce1e62f430e7" "question-34c44cc9-bf3e-5025-8ef7-d8fd637a6eae" "question-b06d01a6-0f9f-5c10-83f5-9d9f497a0fba"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7c674592-16b0-5e5a-b0ac-ce1e62f430e7" :question/id #uuid "7c674592-16b0-5e5a-b0ac-ce1e62f430e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-269369" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{2\\times 3}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)=2({y}^{T}Ax)$ where \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWriting out $L$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\nL={\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}2{a}_{ij}{y}_{i}{x}_{j},\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}=2{y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${∇}_{A}L=2(y\\cdot {x}^{T}).$\n\nEvaluating at the given values $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=2([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}])=2([\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 14 & -7 & 0\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 28 & -14 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8abf474a-1fab-5810-988c-58859ca7b121"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8abf474a-1fab-5810-988c-58859ca7b121" :answer-field/id #uuid "8abf474a-1fab-5810-988c-58859ca7b121" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-298e07ae-5f8c-52b7-8fdb-05f8ff2eb333" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3b2813e9-da8e-59ae-9d0e-61e685a4f322" "answer-f7a8f364-5251-5618-b38b-b49e3fc2960c" "answer-af6ac5dd-6929-5011-8bf3-a504e287864a" "answer-298e07ae-5f8c-52b7-8fdb-05f8ff2eb333" "answer-a2aefe95-7159-51aa-88da-37aecf1ef5f2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b2813e9-da8e-59ae-9d0e-61e685a4f322" :answer/id #uuid "3b2813e9-da8e-59ae-9d0e-61e685a4f322" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7a8f364-5251-5618-b38b-b49e3fc2960c" :answer/id #uuid "f7a8f364-5251-5618-b38b-b4