∘}-\\theta )=$" :question/worked-solution "We know that the cofunction of $\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta $ is $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta ,$ and the angle complementary to ${27}^{∘}-\\theta $ is \n\n$$\n{90}^{∘}-({27}^{∘}-\\theta )={90}^{∘}-{27}^{∘}+\\theta ={63}^{∘}+\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡({27}^{∘}-\\theta )=\\operatorname{tan}⁡({90}^{∘}-({27}^{∘}-\\theta ))=\\operatorname{tan}⁡({63}^{∘}+\\theta ).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-555314da-5e88-5538-91a3-29bd66ea2f89"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-555314da-5e88-5538-91a3-29bd66ea2f89" :answer-field/id #uuid "555314da-5e88-5538-91a3-29bd66ea2f89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-232770a9-261e-542e-9bec-2581712671f9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ffea38d3-c884-5870-9640-07170f484d8c" "answer-41ef6204-53b5-57d1-aff2-d8612595549f" "answer-b0afc406-fee9-55f5-92dc-507c9f3aad2f" "answer-2bbc56e7-2aaf-5e66-b87f-ea39cdff55ec" "answer-232770a9-261e-542e-9bec-2581712671f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ffea38d3-c884-5870-9640-07170f484d8c" :answer/id #uuid "ffea38d3-c884-5870-9640-07170f484d8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡({117}^{∘}-\\theta )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41ef6204-53b5-57d1-aff2-d8612595549f" :answer/id #uuid "41ef6204-53b5-57d1-aff2-d8612595549f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡({63}^{∘}+\\theta )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b0afc406-fee9-55f5-92dc-507c9f3aad2f" :answer/id #uuid "b0afc406-fee9-55f5-92dc-507c9f3aad2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡({117}^{∘}+\\theta )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2bbc56e7-2aaf-5e66-b87f-ea39cdff55ec" :answer/id #uuid "2bbc56e7-2aaf-5e66-b87f-ea39cdff55ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡({117}^{∘}-\\theta )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-232770a9-261e-542e-9bec-2581712671f9" :answer/id #uuid "232770a9-261e-542e-9bec-2581712671f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡({63}^{∘}+\\theta )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073675 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3a13b69c-0da2-5493-86d2-76c8bc977240"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-3a13b69c-0da2-5493-86d2-76c8bc977240" :question/id #uuid "3a13b69c-0da2-5493-86d2-76c8bc977240" :question/math-academy-id "q-76841" :question/problem "If $m∠A=(3x+1)^{∘}$ and $m∠B=(4x-9)^{∘},$ find a value of $x$ that satisfies $\\operatorname{cot}⁡A=\\operatorname{tan}⁡B.$  Suppose that both $∠A$ and $∠B$ are acute." :question/worked-solution "If both angles are acute and $\\operatorname{cot}⁡A=\\operatorname{tan}⁡B,$ then the angles $∠A$ and $∠B$ must be complementary, and we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3x+1)^{∘}+(4x-9)^{∘} & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ (7x-8)^{∘} & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ 7x-8 & =90 \\\\ 7x & =98 \\\\ x & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3954b075-3cbd-547a-ab25-a35f014d84a8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3954b075-3cbd-547a-ab25-a35f014d84a8" :answer-field/id #uuid "3954b075-3cbd-547a-ab25-a35f014d84a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ec8b7699-f736-58a7-a627-e8c62a400d67" :answer-field/choices ["answer-201f479f-c986-5031-a33c-dbafb94414b7" "answer-196e30cc-dd4b-56ea-a0b6-1806966dbb09" "answer-ec8b7699-f736-58a7-a627-e8c62a400d67" "answer-6244bb6c-d4f3-5dc9-b931-a8f929d8ca7e" "answer-80eac182-2d21-5af9-acc3-8bc865bbba69"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-201f479f-c986-5031-a33c-dbafb94414b7" :answer/id #uuid "201f479f-c986-5031-a33c-dbafb94414b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}